            "target_entity_instance": "North Sea Basin",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Here, in a new research project, we investigate how elasmobranch (sharks and rays) communities in the North Sea Basin responded to multi-scale climate warming during the Early Eocene (ca. 53-49 Ma). This interval encompasses both the sustained extreme warmth of the Early Eocene Climatic Optimum (EECO), lasting for millions of years, and short-lived hyperthermal events occurring over tens of thousands of years.",
